: true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Seyi+Vibez+Alubarika&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2026 NSNV INC / EMPIRE"]}, {"t": 3180, "time": "00:53:00", "artist": "Dollar Tookson", "title": null, "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Dollar+Tookson", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dollar+Tookson", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Dollar+Tookson", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Dollar+Tookson", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Dollar+Tookson", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Dollar+Tookson", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Dollar+Tookson&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“I think I'm going to dedicate it to Dola Tuxin himself and showcase a bit of his music.”", "the audio briefly looked like Dlala Thukzin & Nkosazana Daughter - Ubuhle (feat. ilovelethu & Funky Qla), but the presenter said otherwise"]}, {"t": 3291, "time": "00:54:51", "artist": "Dlala Thukzin", "title": "iPlan (feat. Zaba & Sykes)", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Dlala+Thukzin+iPlan+%28feat.+Zaba+%26+Sykes%29", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dlala+Thukzin+iPlan+%28feat.+Zaba+%26+Sykes%29", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Dlala+Thukzin+iPlan+%28feat.+Zaba+%26+Sykes%29", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Dlala+Thukzin+iPlan+%28feat.+Zaba+%26+Sykes%29", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1707025087", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Dlala+Thukzin+iPlan+%28feat.+Zaba+%26+Sykes%29", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Dlala+Thukzin+iPlan+%28feat.+Zaba+%26+Sykes%29&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2023 Dlala Records (PTY) Ltd"]}], "counts": {"high": 0, "mid": 11, "low": 2}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:17:03", "end": "00:18:16", "text": "You are tuned in to The Yanos Show on FBi Radio 94.5 with myself, DJ TeeSoul, back for another week. I hope you're all doing extremely well and I hope you're all enjoying the lovely spring weather. And with the good weather, I feel like there's been a lot of good things that have come with that. There's been a couple of events that have happened in the past few weeks. i think it's been very event filled to say the least in sydney and i do have a bit to share about the last actually just last night if you live in sydney and you're in the ama piano scene the afro house scene the three-step scene you would know that we had the pleasure of having dala tuxin in sydney he's touring australia at the moment but with world tours there are problems but that's something that we can talk about if you stay tuned throughout the show we've got the whole hour together let me know what you've been listening to i don't know where we'll end up by the end of this week's show but you know how it goes it's usually a good time anyways but do stay tuned this is the honor show"}, {"start": "00:43:19", "end": "00:47:35", "text": "You are tuned in to The Honour Show on FBi Radio 94.5 and while I've still got about 15 minutes left, just wanted to talk a bit about, I want to say the last week in the scene, you know I love to talk about what's been happening and yesterday in Sydney we had the pleasure of having Lala Tuxent in Sydney. if you don't know who that is i would like to think he's probably i want to say top five dj producers in the afro house three-step scene he has produced so many great hits that most people would know and for anyone that does know him everyone kind of waits to have that big dollar tookson moment and that's usually in the drop of his songs and we finally got to have that moment in Sydney but that did come with its problems but one thing about Sydney is we're gonna make it happen regardless there was such I want to use the word run around with things like organization in terms of promoters and things like that it gets so techie in that space it can get crazy we had a lot going on people in the venue people were waiting for him to get there there was just I think miscommunication is the best word really I am trying to explain it as nicely as possible but we were a bit worried there for a second is he gonna come is he not gonna come um but he ended up coming in the end and that's a big shout out to Blackout Australia they did their biggest one for Sydney and really saved a night that was already looking to be really good and to kind of substitute for everything that happened across that night we had a lot of local DJs who really stepped up and filled in the gaps where a lot of people really felt okay what's gonna happen at this event right now I paid good money paid a good ticket to see a really good artist and the lineup ended up being so extensive and so amazing in the end and a big massive shout out to all the local DJs that really showed up and showed out yesterday I think I can name all of them right now actually myself and Faisal we played a back-to-back set very impromptu but we personally I think did such a good job it was such a good vibe and I think in the moment it really made sense he is an amazing DJ who else played we had Eric uncle rick and he played back-to-back with dj mishu they played amazingly together we had vic as well played an amazing afro house set really warmed people up for the vibe that dollar tookson was going to bring and we also had at a tune as well he's from new zealand he played really really well as well really helped to fill in a lot of the gaps there was so much happening you just kind of had to be there to know what I'm talking about but again so amazing to see the unity that kind of happens when there's an issue and we solved that so quickly and turned it around and then we had DJ Stokey he rounded it out for the night following Dollar Tookson's set which was 10 out of 10 by the way I think for the weight he really showed out for us at least and it was a good time regardless and it was a lot of unknowns but it ended up happening in the end shout out to Blackout again for really doing their biggest one bringing him out and getting rid of the nerves a lot of people had during that night I hope to see a lot more from them in the space in the scene and also the local DJs I will always always always have good things to say about them and the work they're doing to push the sound forward but in the last 10 minutes I think I'm going to dedicate it to Dola Tuxin himself and showcase a bit of his music. If you don't already know, get ready, you're about to know. But if you don't hear from me, this was The Honor Show. Thank you for tuning in."}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:00:19"}, "track": {"title": "Lasha iBoots At 519", "artists": [{"name": "TNK MusiQ"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:04:00"}, "track": {"title": "Deep Emotions", "artists": [{"name": "Lowbass Djy"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:10:00"}, "track": {"title": "Xakapa", "artists": [{"name": "Lowbass Djy"}, {"name": "HouseXcape & Dj Njabsta"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:16:00"}, "track": {"title": "Thriller (feat. Kabza De Small)", "artists": [{"name": "Shakes & Les & Tycoon"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:22:58"}, "track": {"title": "Slow Poizon (feat. Tycoon 